Subject: [PATCH] Fritchii: the barrier after an in-order buffer copy also orders later transfers (EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_COPY_BARRIER, off by default)

Port of Frizti/Fritchii 15f8e4c5c2 (Frizti), itself zortos293/Lichii#805 commit 8b5be87f79
(jpkto, with Claude Opus 5.5; PR open): "vulkan: order later transfers after a copy that asked for
barriers".

EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_COPY_BARRIER=1 (Common::PeSwitch, exact "1"; unset = T82 exactly: the same
GRAPHICS|COMPUTE destination stages): the post barrier of BufferCacheRuntime::CopyBuffer (in-order
copies that asked for barriers) and of PostCopyBarrier (the downloads, gathers and compute uploads
it closes) also has TRANSFER in its destination stages. Mechanism (upstream): a reordered upload in
a later submission (RecordWithUploadBuffer, which runs ahead of that submission's work) has no
barrier of its own before it, and in-order copies do not count as uses for CanReorderUpload, so when
it writes bytes the older copy wrote, nothing orders the two writes and the older one can land last.
The access masks are unchanged (MEMORY_READ|MEMORY_WRITE already covers transfer writes).

Deviation: Lichii's commit changes CopyBuffer only; Fritchii's also PostCopyBarrier, ported as
Fritchii. ClearBuffer's barrier has the same shape and is left as both upstreams leave it.

Honest value for the PS5: near zero. RADV's waits for a barrier come from the source stage mask
(here TRANSFER: wait for the copy to finish), so the older copy is already done before later work
on the queue starts with or without TRANSFER in the destination; the access masks, which drive the
cache flushes, are unchanged. A spec (validation-layer) fix, not a flash or desync fix on RADV.
No test slot of its own; it can ride along in a safety group.

Checks (VM scratch /tmp/fr2-sr8k, fritchii2-safety_checks.sh, log fritchii2-safety.checks.log):
git apply --check on $R/Eglantine (T82); prepare-vulkan-port.py anchor skips identical (6, among
them the vk_buffer_cache wait-site count, unchanged); the generated vk_buffer_cache_cost.cpp
carries the change; -fsyntax-only with the build's flags: rc=0; an injected error in
PostCopyDstStages is reported.

diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_buffer_cache.cpp b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_buffer_cache.cpp
index 3a3fa51..e878cc6 100644
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_buffer_cache.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_buffer_cache.cpp
@@ -29,6 +29,18 @@
 
 namespace Vulkan {
 namespace {
+// EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_COPY_BARRIER=1 (Fritchii 15f8e4c5c2, port of zortos293/Lichii#805 8b5be87f79 by
+// jpkto; off unless set): the barrier after an in-order buffer copy (CopyBuffer with barriers,
+// PostCopyBarrier) also orders later transfers, not only graphics and compute. A reordered upload
+// of the same bytes in a later submission (RecordWithUploadBuffer, ahead of that submission's
+// work) has no barrier of its own before it, and in-order copies are not uses for
+// CanReorderUpload, so the older copy could land last. Read where the barrier is recorded.
+VkPipelineStageFlags PostCopyDstStages() {
+    static const bool transfers_too = Common::PeSwitch("EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_COPY_BARRIER");
+    return transfers_too ? vk::PIPELINE_STAGE_GRAPHICS_COMPUTE_TRANSFER
+                         : vk::PIPELINE_STAGE_GRAPHICS_COMPUTE;
+}
+
 VkBufferCopy MakeBufferCopy(const VideoCommon::BufferCopy& copy) {
     return VkBufferCopy{
         .srcOffset = copy.src_offset,
@@ -614,8 +626,8 @@ void BufferCacheRuntime::CopyBuffer(VkBuffer dst_buffer, VkBuffer src_buffer,
         }
         cmdbuf.CopyBuffer(src_buffer, dst_buffer, vk_copies);
         if (barrier) {
-            cmdbuf.PipelineBarrier(VK_PIPELINE_STAGE_TRANSFER_BIT,
-                                   vk::PIPELINE_STAGE_GRAPHICS_COMPUTE, 0, WRITE_BARRIER);
+            cmdbuf.PipelineBarrier(VK_PIPELINE_STAGE_TRANSFER_BIT, PostCopyDstStages(), 0,
+                                   WRITE_BARRIER);
         }
     });
 }
@@ -643,8 +655,8 @@ void BufferCacheRuntime::PostCopyBarrier() {
     };
     scheduler.RequestOutsideRenderPassOperationContext();
     scheduler.Record([](vk::CommandBuffer cmdbuf) {
-        cmdbuf.PipelineBarrier(VK_PIPELINE_STAGE_TRANSFER_BIT, vk::PIPELINE_STAGE_GRAPHICS_COMPUTE,
-                               0, WRITE_BARRIER);
+        cmdbuf.PipelineBarrier(VK_PIPELINE_STAGE_TRANSFER_BIT, PostCopyDstStages(), 0,
+                               WRITE_BARRIER);
     });
 }
 
